0..76 Comment "/// This source states that a literal identity test computes while a type is"
77..89 Comment "/// checked."
90..93 Comment "///"
94..161 Comment "/// A type that decodes a name to a code compares two texts, so the"
162..232 Comment "/// comparison of two literals must compute while the type is checked."
233..236 Comment "///"
237..311 Comment "/// Equality of two integers or two texts, and inequality of two integers,"
312..386 Comment "/// gives the boolean that the identity of the literals gives. The checker"
387..465 Comment "/// computes each test, and the kernel computes it again by its own comparison"
466..540 Comment "/// of the literals. A test over a parameter stays a call, and every other"
541..575 Comment "/// native operation stays opaque."
576..579 Comment "///"
580..629 Comment "/// - see: #6142 — `texts_same`, `decoded_flag`"
630..696 Comment "/// - see: #6158 — `decoded_flag`, a comparison in a stated type"
